  "scope": "# Review \u2014 3f533a120cf5\n\nTask/source: `3f533a120cf5`, generator SHA-256 `c63333b9cd8acc75cd147d76deff12590f9267cb7286d9d18f14cddf2bf8cd5c`, canonical rule hash `df7e059f3faa`.\nStatus: **complete, routine task-local prototype**; no production generator or canonical Racket bytes changed.\nNeed \u2192 repair: the approved original family lacked parametric evidence, so I built a runnable two-parameter paint-semantics prototype rather than altering its authority.\nPrototype: `key_target={gray_cells,bbox_holes}` and `key_order={forward,reverse}`; `gray_cells/forward` is the exact canonical default.\nEpisode contract: one setting per seed, 2 demonstrations, 4 distinct queries, exact retained Racket for every label, and demo-only elimination of all three declared rivals.\nPublic boundary: visible-byte-derived opaque IDs; public JSON excludes settings, seeds, Racket, and query answers.\nVerification: the staged assigned-task runner passed **17/17 tests**; retained batch replay reports all settings covered, all labels matching Racket, all queries identified, and valid public projection.\nTest repair: the issued legacy test used a nonportable fixed parent depth; it now uses `reviewer_support.find_root/canonical_path` and passes in the staged runtime.\nTickets: both bounded probes completed; API override behavior matched its declared boundary, and the pinned `04a27ff51304` ambiguity reproduced exactly while remaining unresolved.\nRemaining limit: the rival proof is finite to the four declared settings; this prototype is not production approval or training admission.",
